hout a receipt when the ledger includes a note.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/01_allowability_rules.md","text":"# Allowability Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-20\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated award document for the reimbursement cap when award documents conflict.\n- Expense eligibility comes from these current allowability rules.\n\n## Reimbursement Rules\n\n- Garden supplies are eligible.\n- Accessibility printing and accessibility services are eligible.\n- Public outreach postage is eligible.\n- Volunteer refreshments are eligible up to `$120.00` for this event.\n- Staff gifts are not eligible.\n- Fines and penalties are not eligible.\n- A receipt is required for any single expense over `$75.00`.\n- Expenses of `$75.00` or less may be approved without a receipt when the ledger includes a note.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":19,"totalLines":19,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/01_allowability_rules.md","time":{"start":1781410243258,"end":1781410243306}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_02a0153f46c007fd016a2e29c311c8819187f38b1da31fa705"}},"id":"prt_ec45322b7001J67Lx9tKfSueRh","sessionID":"ses_13bad1c5effesdbGz2xBQiO0IK","messageID":"msg_ec452fe22001hW1E5BxCp6dxpu"}}
