equested amount | Approved amount | Decision | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| G-001 | 980.00 | 980.00 | approve | Garden supplies are eligible. Receipt is on file for this expense over `$75.00`. |\n+| G-002 | 145.00 | 120.00 | partial | Volunteer refreshments are eligible only up to the `$120.00` event cap. |\n+| G-003 | 420.00 | 420.00 | approve | Accessibility printing is eligible. Receipt is on file for this expense over `$75.00`. |\n+| G-004 | 160.00 | 0.00 | reject | Staff gifts are not eligible. |\n+| G-005 | 310.00 | 0.00 | reject | Public outreach printing is not listed as an eligible cost under the current rules. It also exceeds `$75.00` and has no receipt on file, so the receipt rule would independently block reimbursement. |\n+| G-006 | 68.00 | 68.00 | approve | Public outreach postage is eligible. Because the amount is `$75.00` or less and the ledger includes a note, it may be approved without a receipt. |\n+\n+## Rule Applications\n+\n+- Volunteer refreshments cap applied to `G-002`: maximum reimbursable amount is `$120.00`.\n+- Receipt rule applied to `G-001` and `G-003`: both exceed `$75.00` and have receipts on file.\n+- Receipt rule applied to `G-005`: the expense exceeds `$75.00` and has no receipt, so it cannot be approved.\n+- Receipt rule applied to `G-006`: the expense is `$75.00` or less and includes a ledger note, so it can be approved without a receipt.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/grant_closeout_recovery/answer/final_closeout_summary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+# Final Closeout Summary\n+\n+The corrected reimbursement cap for this closeout is `$1,600.00`, based on `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That award update is the newest dated aw